      "abstractions": [
        "Two accounts and seven connection generations; account changes, reconnects and searches are disabled at the generation bound rather than dropped.",
        "Failure codes are three classes: transient (unavailable, invalid-response, timeout), offline, and unauthorized (which also stands for every other code that is not retried). The retry delay table is a counter that saturates at four; the delays are nondeterministic timer ticks.",
        "The one-minute limit on unforced attempts is a flag set by an attempt and cleared by a nondeterministic tick. A stored sign-in at launch is the first account change.",
        "Guidance is one flag owned by the Maps screen: uninstalling the installed provider releases the screen and ends it; activating a provider on an unconfigured screen does not.",
        "The retry timer callback forces a connection. A timer left armed across a connection the Maps screen started for a search therefore replaces that working connection: TimerKeepsGuidanceDesired is outside safety and retryTimerAfterSearchReplacesProviderTest replays it.",
        "A connection the Maps screen starts itself does not arm a retry when it fails transiently: EveryTransientFailureHasRetryDesired is outside safety and searchFailureArmsNoRetryTest replays it.",
        "retryProgress is a temporal property under weak fairness of the timer; the default gate typechecks it and simulation checks the state invariant TransientFailureHasRetry. The regional provider and map-plane retry are not modeled."
      ]
    },
