        "Six message identifiers. A message is the user's or an agent reply whose newest card Maps can open; card parsing, the parse cache and share-choice answers are not modeled.",
        "A replaced or restored history is one or two messages with new identifiers, each carrying a result. A new shell object is a remount with no Seen record.",
        "The open itself is a recorded request; whether Maps accepts it, and whether the owner preference then starts guidance, is in MapsNavigation.",
        "A reply that arrives in a conversation whose previous render was empty, or between a history replacement and the next render, does not open; the model keeps that."
      ]
