      "abstractions": [
        "Three sessions and three instruction texts. Bridge calls are one first-in first-out queue handled by the native service; the availability read and listener registration are separate resolutions.",
        "start() stops a leftover session and takes the new one in a single step: its callers always stop the previous session first, so that wait is one microtask.",
        "A native start may be refused; an update may be refused or find another session. The notification's Stop, a refused service and a removed task are one native end event; AlphaNavigationService's per-reason handling is in NavigationProgress.",
        "Unsupported platforms, where start() resolves false without a session, are the availability refusal."
      ]
    },
